Constraints:
- Produce exactly one card per beat, in the same order as card_ids.
- Generate the full stage in one response; do not split or stream per-card outputs.
- Treat the deck as a readable portrait of the world at this stage.
- Most cards should be straightforward world-state facts:
  - what changed
  - who feels it
  - how it shows up in ordinary life or institutional behavior
- Avoid making standard cards read like "if X then Y" rules text. That should be uncommon.
- Make the writing accessible to a lay audience: short, concrete, and vivid without sounding sensational.
- Favor broader social and economic stories over technical details.
- Ensure many developments show realistic AI effects in the economy: work, wages, prices, services, energy, logistics, trust, security, and trade.
- Keep early stages especially grounded in present-day or near-term developments.
- In mid and late stages, include some bigger shifts in institutions or strategic doctrine, but always tie them back to real-world effects people can understand.
- Include a mix of positive, mixed, and negative cards with a generally optimistic skew.
- Most standard cards should have rule_box_text = null and activation.type = immediate.
- Conditional standard cards should be rare and use broad policy hooks only.
- Power cards should be rare, simple, and legible:
  - description = the world-state event
  - rule_box_text = the imperative rule sentence
  - effects = one or two simple gameplay effects
- Keep dependencies broad and interpretable. Players should be able to judge them without legalistic rules parsing.
- Respect any special_directive in the beat object.
- For supersedes, describe a natural progression or reversal of an earlier story in plain language.
- For quantitative_indicator, use understandable indicators such as prices, wait times, unemployment, adoption rates, or throughput.
- Title: 2-4 words, simple and plain-language.
- short_description: <= 60 characters.
- description: 1 short sentence, <= 180 characters total for standard cards.
- impact_score: integer from -5 to 5. Use mostly 0 to 3 in magnitude. Reserve 4s and 5s for rare breaks.
- Map impact_score to icons exactly: positive uses arrows_up only, negative uses arrows_down only, zero uses neither.
- severity reflects how consequential the development is for the game state, not how alarming the prose sounds.
- Do NOT put raw tag ids or technical shorthand into the text shown to players.
- art_prompt should match the world story and specify an edge-to-edge landscape illustration that fills the entire frame.

